<Song resolves-to="SongSP" spName="NowsTheTime-F-Theme" spTempo="180">
  <spVERSION>4</spVERSION>
  <spComments>Year:	1945
Composer:	Charlie Parker
Lyricist:	None — instrumental
Form:	12-bar blues
Style:	Bebop jazz blues
Key:	F major

“Now’s the Time” is a riff-based blues composed and first
recorded by Charlie Parker on November 26, 1945. Its compact,
blues-rooted melody reflects Parker’s Kansas City influences
while incorporating bebop phrasing; the tune later became the
basis for the hit “The Hucklebuck,” which was credited to Andy
Gibson rather than Parker. </spComments>
